DISABLED (.patch.disabled -- Buildroot only auto-applies *.patch).

Kept for the record: masking ONLY the ext-adv feature bit puts the kernel
on legacy advertising while it still uses EXTENDED scan/connect commands
(use_ext_scan/use_ext_conn key off the supported-commands bitmap, not this
feature bit). Controllers reject that mix, and on the AIC8800D80 it killed
LE scanning outright (0 devices vs 65 before) and left connections failing
with le-connection-abort-by-local. If a fully-legacy stack is ever needed,
this patch must ALSO clear supported-commands octet 37 bits 0x20/0x40/0x80
(LE Set Extended Scan Parameters/Enable, LE Extended Create Connection) in
the Read Local Supported Commands (0x1002) complete event.

Original rationale follows.

Mask the AIC8800D80's LE Extended Advertising feature bit: the firmware
claims the feature and ACKs every ext-adv HCI command, but never
transmits ext-adv PDUs on air; legacy advertising works (device-proven
on the Radxa Dragon Q6A, 2026-07-25 -- see the WiFi/Bluetooth section
of the target README). Masking le_features[1] bit 4 in the LE Read
Local Supported Features command-complete keeps the kernel and BlueZ
on the legacy advertising path. Applied by Buildroot's automatic package-patch step (BEFORE the debian
series replay in aic8800.mk; conflict-free -- the only series patch touching this file, fix-usb-firmware-path.patch, is skipped).

--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic_btusb/aic_btusb.c	2026-07-25 20:59:51.796626875 +0000
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic_btusb/aic_btusb.c	2026-07-25 20:59:51.797626890 +0000
@@ -3850,6 +3850,25 @@
 
         if (bt_cb(skb)->expect == 0) {
             /* Complete frame */
+            if (skb->len >= 14 &&
+                skb->data[0] == HCI_EV_CMD_COMPLETE &&
+                skb->data[3] == 0x03 && skb->data[4] == 0x20 &&
+                skb->data[5] == 0x00) {
+                /* LE Read Local Supported Features complete: the
+                 * AIC8800D80 firmware claims LE Extended Advertising
+                 * support, and the controller ACKs every ext-adv HCI
+                 * command (LE Set Extended Advertising Params/Data/
+                 * Enable all return status 0x00) -- but no ext-adv PDU
+                 * is ever transmitted on air, while the legacy
+                 * advertising commands (0x2006/0x2008/0x200A) transmit
+                 * fine (device-proven on Dragon Q6A, 2026-07-25).
+                 * Kernel 7.1 has no HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_EXT_ADV, so mask
+                 * the feature bit (le_features[1] bit 4) here in the
+                 * event path; the kernel and BlueZ then stay on the
+                 * working legacy advertising path (max_adv_len 31).
+                 */
+                skb->data[7] &= ~0x10;
+            }
             hci_recv_frame(data->hdev, skb);
             skb = NULL;
         }
